@node About Majutsu
@section About Majutsu

Majutsu shows a Jujutsu repository in Emacs buffers: the log@comma{} diffs@comma{} files
as of a revision@comma{} bookmarks@comma{} operations.  Commands start from what is at
point@comma{} and most open a transient in which you pick revisions from the log
before anything runs.  It is built on Magit's sections and on the Transient
package@comma{} so it will feel familiar to Magit users.

@node About Jujutsu
@section About Jujutsu

Jujutsu (jj) is a version control system whose working copy is represented by a
commit. Unlike Git@comma{} it has no staging area: the working-copy commit is marked
@samp{@@}@comma{} and jj snapshots filesystem changes into it at the beginning of most
commands. Mutable history and conflicts are first-class parts of Jujutsu's
model@comma{} making rebasing@comma{} squashing@comma{} and conflict resolution ordinary operations.

