@node Sections
@section Sections

Majutsu organizes information into collapsible sections.  @code{TAB} toggles the
section at point@comma{} such as a revision description in the log or a file in a
diff.

@strong{Vanilla:} @code{n} and @code{p} move forward and backward through sections.

@strong{Evil:} @code{C-j} and @code{C-k} move forward and backward through sections in Normal@comma{}
Visual@comma{} and Motion states; @code{g j} and @code{g k} move between siblings.

@node Transients
@section Transients

Commands are grouped into transients: popup menus@comma{} built with Emacs'
Transient package@comma{} in which you set options before running a command.
@code{r}@comma{} for example@comma{} opens the Rebase transient.

The main action of a transient has its own key and also runs on @code{RET};
customize @code{majutsu-transient-default-action} to use another key.

@menu
* Saved Defaults::
@end menu

@node Saved Defaults
@subsection Saved Defaults

The Log@comma{} Diff@comma{} operation log@comma{} Fetch@comma{} Push@comma{} and Gerrit Upload transients can
remember their options.  @code{w} opens the defaults transient:

@multitable {aaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Key
@tab Saves the options for
@tab Cleared by
@item @code{w u}
@tab the user
@tab @code{w U}
@item @code{w r}
@tab this repository
@tab @code{w R}
@item @code{w w}
@tab this workspace
@tab @code{w W}
@end multitable

@code{s} sets the options for this workspace until Emacs exits.  The most
specific layer wins: session@comma{} workspace@comma{} repository@comma{} user@comma{} built-in.  A
layer replaces the whole option list; layers are not merged.

Saving does not run the command.  One-off values@comma{} such as the revisions of
a diff or the bookmarks of a push@comma{} are not saved.  In the Log transient@comma{} @code{0}
resets the options of the current buffer and leaves saved defaults alone.

A log or diff buffer that is already open keeps its own options.
@code{majutsu-prefix-use-buffer-arguments} and
@code{majutsu-direct-use-buffer-arguments} decide when a transient or a direct
command starts from them.

The defaults are stored in @code{transient-values-file}@comma{} not in jj's
configuration.  Additional workspaces share the repository layer and have
their own workspace layer.

@node Selecting Revisions
@section Selecting Revisions

Transients that take revisions@comma{} such as Rebase@comma{} Squash@comma{} or Diff@comma{} let you pick
them in the log.  An entry shown as @samp{-r/r} has two keys: @samp{-r} reads a revset
in the minibuffer@comma{} and @code{r} toggles the revision at point.  Selected
revisions stay highlighted@comma{} one color per role@comma{} until the command runs or
@code{c} clears them.

For example@comma{} to rebase a change onto another:
@table @asis
@item @code{n n}
Move to the change to rebase.
@item @code{r}
Open the Rebase transient.  The log stays live under it.
@item @code{s}
Mark the revision at point as the source.
@item @code{n n}
Move to where it should go.
@item @code{o}
Mark that revision as the destination.
@item @code{RET}
Run the rebase; Majutsu asks first.
@item @code{y}
The change and its descendants now sit on the destination.
@end table

With an active region@comma{} an argument that can be repeated takes every
revision in the region; an argument that takes one value uses one revision.
Majutsu passes revisions@comma{} not expressions: it does not turn a region into
@samp{A..B}.  Type such revsets at the @samp{-r} prompt.

Without a selection@comma{} a command uses the revision at point@comma{} or the default
its own section of this manual names.

@node Filesets
@section Filesets

The @samp{--} entry of a transient limits the command to some files.  It reads jj
fileset expressions@comma{} several separated by commas:

@example
src/main.el@comma{} docs
glob:"**/*.org"
src & ~glob:"**/*-test.el"
@end example

Completion works on the path being typed@comma{} wherever it is in the expression@comma{}
and offers the pattern kinds@comma{} such as @samp{glob:} and @samp{root:}@comma{} where a pattern
can start.  Anything you type is accepted.

Diff@comma{} Split@comma{} Squash@comma{} Absorb@comma{} and Restore complete the paths that the transient's
revisions change@comma{} since those are the only ones the command can act on.
Log completes any path@comma{} one directory level at a time@comma{} so a large
repository is never listed whole.

@node Completion and Confirmation
@section Completion and Confirmation

Prompts use Emacs' completion@comma{} so Vertico@comma{} Ivy@comma{} and similar interfaces
work.  Revset prompts complete whole expressions with candidates from jj and
label each one with its kind@comma{} such as bookmark@comma{} tag@comma{} or workspace.

Destructive commands such as Abandon@comma{} Undo@comma{} and Restore ask first; see
@ref{Customizing, , Confirmation Settings}.

@node Running jj
@section Running jj

Every jj command Majutsu runs is recorded@comma{} with its output@comma{} in the
repository's process buffer.  Fetch@comma{} Push@comma{} Gerrit upload@comma{} diff editors@comma{} and
anything that waits for an editor run in the background; other commands
finish before control returns.

