@node Log Display
@subsection Log Display

Each revision is a section.  Its first line shows the change id@comma{} bookmarks@comma{}
tags@comma{} and the first line of the description@comma{} with the commit id@comma{} author@comma{} and
date aligned to the right.  The rest of a description is the section's body;
@code{TAB} folds it.

The graph is jj's.  Lines between revisions@comma{} such as @samp{(elided revisions)}@comma{}
are decoration: point skips them@comma{} and they are neither searched nor copied.

A description too long for the window is cut with … so that the right-hand
columns stay aligned.  Only the display is cut; set
@code{majutsu-log-elide-description} to nil to show descriptions in full.

In the jjosh build a revision also lists the projects it touches@comma{} such as
@samp{[appkit@comma{} chidu]}.  Customize @code{majutsu-log-template-touched-projects} to
change the format.

The columns are configurable; see @ref{Log Columns, , Log Columns}.

@table @asis
@item @kbd{n} (@code{majutsu-goto-next-revision})
@kindex n
@findex majutsu-goto-next-revision
Move to the next revision in display order.
@item @kbd{p} (@code{majutsu-goto-prev-revision})
@kindex p
@findex majutsu-goto-prev-revision
Move to the previous revision in display order.
@end table

@table @asis
@item @kbd{[} (@code{majutsu-log-goto-parent})
@kindex [
@findex majutsu-log-goto-parent
Jump to a visible parent.  With several
  parents@comma{} choose one; candidates show the description.
@item @kbd{]} (@code{majutsu-log-goto-child})
@kindex ]
@findex majutsu-log-goto-child
