@item
@anchor{Understanding @samp{--revisions}}Understanding @samp{--revisions}


The @samp{--revisions} argument accepts any revset that forms a @emph{contiguous} set of
commits. "Contiguous" means no gaps in the DAG@comma{} but @strong{forks and merges are
allowed}.

Examples:
@table @asis
@item @samp{-r @@}
Changes in the working copy commit (default).
@item @samp{-r @@-}
Changes in the parent of the working copy.
@item @samp{-r B::D}
Total changes from B through D@.
@item @samp{-r 'A | B'}
Valid only if A and B form a contiguous set; gaps produce an error.
@end table

When visiting a file from such a diff@comma{} Majutsu uses the exact range stored by
the diff buffer:
@itemize
@item
On an @strong{added} or @strong{context} line: resolve the @samp{--revisions} expression itself.
@item
On a @strong{removed} line: resolve the parents of that expression
(@samp{REVSET-} in revset syntax).
@end itemize

Blob buffers require that the chosen side resolve to exactly one revision.
Majutsu reports an error rather than arbitrarily choosing one head or root.

@strong{Note}: When the revset has multiple heads or roots@comma{} the target revision for
file visits may be ambiguous. For example@comma{} in an X-shaped history:
@example
D   E       <- two heads
 \ /
  C
 / \
A   B       <- two roots
@end example
If you diff @samp{-r A::D | B::E}@comma{} there are two heads (D@comma{} E) and two roots (A@comma{} B).
The diff shows changes from the @emph{merged} parents to the @emph{merged} heads. If D
and E modify the same lines@comma{} the diff can show conflict markers. Inspection of
the combined diff still works@comma{} but visiting a blob from either ambiguous side
fails the single-revision check. Use @samp{--from} / @samp{--to} with single revisions
when precise file navigation matters.

@item
@anchor{Diff Buffer}Diff Buffer


The diff of one revision starts with that revision's metadata and its full
description@comma{} both collapsible.  A @samp{--from} / @samp{--to} comparison@comma{} or a revset
of several revisions@comma{} shows only the diff.

A stat summary is a collapsible directory tree: single-directory chains are
joined@comma{} and a rename appears under its destination with the source path in
the file's folded body.

