@node File and Blob Inspection
@subsection File and Blob Inspection

A blob buffer shows one file as of one revision.

@deffn Command majutsu-find-file
Prompt for revset + path (defaulting from point
  when possible) and open that file as a blob.
@end deffn

@deffn Command majutsu-find-file-other-window
Like @code{majutsu-find-file}@comma{} but
  display the blob in another window.
@end deffn

@deffn Command majutsu-find-file-other-frame
Like @code{majutsu-find-file}@comma{} but
  display the blob in another frame.
@end deffn

Opening a file resolves its revset once and identifies the blob by workspace@comma{}
full commit ID@comma{} and path. Different versions of one change have separate
buffers. Revision actions@comma{} including Restore and Ediff@comma{} use the displayed
commit@comma{} not a newer version of the same change.

Explicit refresh resolves the original revset again. Missing files@comma{}
unsupported tree values@comma{} and warning-only reads leave the previous contents@comma{}
commit pin@comma{} and refresh target intact. Regular files and text file conflicts
are supported@comma{} including empty files; symlinks@comma{} submodules@comma{} and structural
conflicts are not blob-editing inputs.

Blob buffers are read-only snapshots with history-aware navigation:
