@node Creating Changes
@section Creating Changes

@table @asis
@item @kbd{o} (@code{majutsu-new})
@kindex o
@findex majutsu-new
Open the New transient to specify options.
@end table

Direct log-buffer shortcuts:
@table @asis
@item @kbd{O} (@code{majutsu-new-dwim})
@kindex O
@findex majutsu-new-dwim
Create a new change on top of the revision at point (DWIM).
@item @kbd{A} (@code{majutsu-new-with-after})
@kindex A
@findex majutsu-new-with-after
Create a new change after the revision at point.
@item @kbd{B (Vanilla)} (@code{majutsu-new-with-before})
@kindex B (Vanilla)
@findex majutsu-new-with-before
Create a new change before the revision at point.
@item @kbd{I (Evil)} (@code{majutsu-new-with-before})
@kindex I (Evil)
@findex majutsu-new-with-before
Create a new change before the revision at point.
@end table

Where the new change goes@comma{} with the revision at point marked:
@table @asis
@item On top (@code{O})
@example
@@  wqnwkozp (no description set)
│ ○  xzyvoorv Add the renderer
├─╯
○  mxtrukyy Polish the index  ← at point
○  vzxpmxlw Import the parser core
@end example
The new change is a child of the revision at point.  Its other children
stay where they are.
@item After (@code{A})
@example
○  xzyvoorv Add the renderer  ← rebased
@@  wqnwkozp (no description set)
○  mxtrukyy Polish the index  ← at point
○  vzxpmxlw Import the parser core
@end example
The new change goes between the revision at point and its children@comma{} which
are rebased onto it.
@item Before (@code{B}@comma{} Evil @code{I})
@example
○  xzyvoorv Add the renderer  ← rebased
○  mxtrukyy Polish the index  ← at point@comma{} rebased
@@  wqnwkozp (no description set)
○  vzxpmxlw Import the parser core
@end example
The new change goes between the revision at point and its parents.  The
revision at point and its descendants are rebased onto it.
@end table

Useful transient entries include:
@table @asis
@item @kbd{-r}
@kindex -r
Parent revisions.
@item @kbd{-A}
@kindex -A
Insert after constraint.
@item @kbd{-B}
@kindex -B
Insert before constraint.
@item @kbd{-m}
@kindex -m
Set a message.
@item @kbd{-e}
@kindex -e
No edit (don't switch to the new change).
@end table
Runs: @samp{jj new -r REV}

