@node Description Buffer
@subsection Description Buffer

jj waits while you edit the description in Emacs.  Finish to let jj use the
text@comma{} or cancel to make jj abort the command.

@table @asis
@item @kbd{C-c C-c} (@code{with-editor-finish})
@kindex C-c C-c
@findex with-editor-finish
Finish; jj uses the description.
@item @kbd{C-c C-k} (@code{with-editor-cancel})
@kindex C-c C-k
@findex with-editor-cancel
Cancel; jj aborts the command.  The
  text is kept in the description history.
@item @kbd{C-c C-d} (@code{majutsu-jjdescription-show-diff})
@kindex C-c C-d
@findex majutsu-jjdescription-show-diff
Show the diff of the
  change being described.
@end table

Lines that start with @code{JJ:} are comments@comma{} and everything after
@code{JJ: ignore-rest} is ignored.  Summary text beyond column 68 is highlighted
and the body fills at column 72; see
@ref{Customizing, , Description Options}.

Majutsu remembers the descriptions of the session.  Recalling one replaces
the description and keeps jj's comments.  The history is not available when
several revisions are described in one buffer.

@table @asis
@item @kbd{M-p} (@code{majutsu-jjdescription-prev-message})
@kindex M-p
@findex majutsu-jjdescription-prev-message
Recall the previous
  description.  A numeric prefix goes back that many.
@item @kbd{M-n} (@code{majutsu-jjdescription-next-message})
@kindex M-n
@findex majutsu-jjdescription-next-message
Recall the next
  description.
@item @kbd{C-c M-p} (@code{majutsu-jjdescription-search-message-backward})
@kindex C-c M-p
@findex majutsu-jjdescription-search-message-backward
Search
  backward through the history for a substring.
@item @kbd{C-c M-n} (@code{majutsu-jjdescription-search-message-forward})
@kindex C-c M-n
@findex majutsu-jjdescription-search-message-forward
Search
  forward through the history for a substring.
@item @kbd{C-c M-s} (@code{majutsu-jjdescription-save-message})
@kindex C-c M-s
@findex majutsu-jjdescription-save-message
Save the current text
  to the history.
@end table

@node Editing Descriptions in Place
@subsection Editing Descriptions in Place

Descriptions can also be edited where they are displayed: in the log@comma{} and
above the diff of one revision.  Like Wdired@comma{} a session makes every
description in the buffer editable while the rest stays read-only@comma{} so
several revisions can be reworded at once.

@table @asis
@item @kbd{w (Vanilla)} (@code{majutsu-section-edit})
@kindex w (Vanilla)
@findex majutsu-section-edit
Start editing.
@item @kbd{i (Evil)} (@code{majutsu-evil-section-edit})
@kindex i (Evil)
@findex majutsu-evil-section-edit
Start editing and stay in
  Normal state; a second @code{i} enters Insert state.
@end table

@table @asis
@item @kbd{C-c C-c} (@code{majutsu-section-edit-finish})
@kindex C-c C-c
@findex majutsu-section-edit-finish
Apply every changed
  description in one @samp{jj describe}.
@item @kbd{C-c C-k} (@code{majutsu-section-edit-abort})
@kindex C-c C-k
@findex majutsu-section-edit-abort
Discard the edits.
@item @kbd{C-x C-q} (@code{majutsu-section-edit-exit})
@kindex C-x C-q
@findex majutsu-section-edit-exit
Leave; if anything changed@comma{} ask
  whether to apply it.
@item @kbd{Z Z / Z Q (Evil)} (@code{majutsu-section-edit-finish / majutsu-section-edit-abort})
@kindex Z Z / Z Q (Evil)
@findex majutsu-section-edit-finish / majutsu-section-edit-abort
Apply or discard.  @code{:w} applies too@comma{} and @code{<escape>} leaves like @code{C-x C-q}.
@end table

The cursor changes while a session is active
(@code{majutsu-section-edit-cursor-type}).  Descriptions cut for alignment are
shown in full.

