@node Absorbing
@section Absorbing

@table @asis
@item @kbd{a} (@code{majutsu-absorb})
@kindex a
@findex majutsu-absorb
Open the Absorb transient.
@end table

Arguments:
@table @asis
@item @kbd{-f}
@kindex -f
Source revision (@samp{--from}@comma{} default @samp{@@}).
@item @kbd{-t}
@kindex -t
Destination revset filters (@samp{--into}@comma{} repeatable@comma{} default @samp{mutable()}).
@item @kbd{-i}
@kindex -i
Open jj's configured diff editor for partial selection.
@item @kbd{@code{=t}}
@kindex @code{=t}
Choose jj's diff editor with @samp{--tool=NAME} (implies interactive).
@item @kbd{--}
@kindex --
Limit absorb to @ref{Filesets, , filesets}.
@end table
Runs: @samp{jj absorb --from REV --into REVSETS... [FILESETS...]}

From a single-revision Diff buffer@comma{} use @code{H} to select a hunk@comma{} @code{F} for a file
or directory@comma{} and @code{R} for a region within a hunk; @code{C} clears these selections.
Press @code{a} or @code{RET} to absorb the selection using Majutsu's patch tool@comma{} without
enabling @samp{-i}.  The selection can span files; opening the transient at a file
does not narrow it to that file.  Existing diff fileset limits still apply.

Only selected changes are considered for absorption.  jj assigns them to the
closest eligible ancestors@comma{} restricted by @samp{--into}.  Unselected changes and
changes jj cannot assign remain in the source revision.  Explicit @samp{-i} or
@samp{--tool} requests instead use jj's diff editor@comma{} as described under
@ref{Interactive Patching, , Interactive Patching}.

