@node Arranging
@section Arranging

@code{majutsu-arrange-tui} runs jj's full-screen @samp{arrange} command inside Emacs@comma{}
in a Ghostel terminal.  It is @code{? A} in the dispatcher; @code{A} in the log itself
is @code{majutsu-new-with-after}.

Without a prefix argument it runs @samp{jj arrange}@comma{} and jj's @samp{revsets.arrange}
setting chooses the revisions.  With a prefix argument@comma{} Majutsu asks for a
revset.

Arrange needs a terminal@comma{} so Ghostel is required.  It works in local
repositories and over TRAMP to POSIX hosts.  When the TUI exits@comma{} the buffer
that started it is refreshed and the terminal transcript stays available.

