@node Selecting
@subsection Selecting

Open the diff of the revision (@code{RET})@comma{} then the transient of the command (@code{S}@comma{}
@code{s}@comma{} @code{a}@comma{} or @code{R}).  A Patch Selection group appears:

@multitable {aaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Key
@tab Command
@tab Toggles
@item @code{H}
@tab @code{majutsu-interactive-toggle-hunk}
@tab the hunk at point
@item @code{F}
@tab @code{majutsu-interactive-toggle-file}
@tab a file@comma{} or everything below a stat-summary directory
@item @code{R}
@tab @code{majutsu-interactive-toggle-region}
@tab the lines in the region
@item @code{C}
@tab @code{majutsu-interactive-clear}
@tab clears the whole selection
@end multitable

Selected hunks@comma{} lines@comma{} and files are highlighted@comma{} and the stat summary shows
which files are selected in full or in part.  On a directory@comma{} @code{F} selects
every file below it@comma{} folded ones included; on a fully selected directory it
clears them.

Run the command with its usual key or @code{RET}.  Only the selection is acted
on:

@multitable {aaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Command
@tab Selected changes
@tab Everything else
@item Split
@tab go to the first commit
@tab stays in the second
@item Squash
@tab move to the destination
@tab stays in the source
@item Absorb
@tab are offered to jj@comma{} which assigns them to ancestors
@tab stays in the source
@item Restore
@tab are undone
@tab is left alone
@end multitable

Absorb leaves selected changes that jj cannot assign in the source too;
@samp{--into} limits the ancestors it considers.

A selection cannot be carried to another command; clear it first.

For example@comma{} to squash only the changes to one file into the parent: open
the revision's diff with @code{RET}@comma{} press @code{s}@comma{} press @code{F} on the file@comma{} and run the
squash.

@node Which Diffs Work
@subsection Which Diffs Work

The diff must show what the command acts on:

@itemize
@item
Split and Absorb need the diff of one revision.
@item
Squash needs the diff of one revision@comma{} which becomes the source.  Without
a destination@comma{} Majutsu squashes into its parent.
@item
Restore takes the diff of one revision@comma{} as @samp{--changes-in}@comma{} or a
@samp{--from} / @samp{--to} comparison.
@end itemize

File limits of the diff still apply.  A selection whose diff has changed
since is rejected instead of being applied to other content.  Only one
patch operation@comma{} terminal editor@comma{} or blob save writes to a workspace at a
time; a second one is refused until the first ends.

@node jj's Diff Editors
@subsection jj's Diff Editors

@samp{-i} and @code{=t} (@samp{--tool=NAME}) choose in another way: they start jj's own
diff editor.  They take precedence over an Emacs selection@comma{} which is kept.
Note that @samp{-t} is a destination option@comma{} not short for @samp{--tool}.

jj's default editor@comma{} @samp{:builtin}@comma{} is a terminal program.
@code{majutsu-diff-editor-host} decides where editors run:

@table @asis
@item @samp{auto}
The default: Ghostel when it is installed@comma{} otherwise an
ordinary process.
@item @samp{ghostel}
Always Ghostel.  Runs the built-in editor and other terminal
tools.
@item @samp{process}
For tools that open their own window; @samp{:builtin} is refused.
@end table

Ghostel is optional and also works over TRAMP to POSIX hosts.  When Split
or Squash goes on to ask for a description@comma{} it opens in Emacs as usual;
locally this needs a working @samp{emacsclient}.

@node Limits
@subsection Limits

@itemize
@item
A deleted file is selected whole or not at all.
@item
Changes without text hunks@comma{} such as binary files and mode changes@comma{} are
selected as whole files with @code{F}@comma{} for Split@comma{} Squash@comma{} and Restore@comma{} in a
Git-format diff.
@item
The mode change of a copied file cannot be kept without the copy.
@item
Hunks in new and renamed files are selected like any others.
@end itemize

